n=\"-7.23s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><rect x=\"-3.9\" y=\"-6.3\" width=\"7.8\" height=\"12.5\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#c8302f\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"360\" dur=\"3.45s\" begin=\"-7.23s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"541,-20; 566,150; 541,320\" dur=\"6.97s\" begin=\"-3.35s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><circle r=\"4.2\" fill=\"#e8b100\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"720\" dur=\"3.48s\" begin=\"-3.35s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"354,-20; 343,150; 354,320\" dur=\"6.56s\" begin=\"-1.91s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><rect x=\"-4.4\" y=\"-7.5\" width=\"8.8\" height=\"15.0\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#7a4fa0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"-360\" dur=\"3.28s\" begin=\"-1.91s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"490,-20; 510,150; 490,320\" dur=\"5.01s\" begin=\"-4.12s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><rect x=\"-3.1\" y=\"-6.9\" width=\"6.1\" height=\"13.7\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#7a4fa0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"-720\" dur=\"2.51s\" begin=\"-4.12s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"574,-20; 590,150; 574,320\" dur=\"3.78s\" begin=\"-2.02s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><circle r=\"5.1\" fill=\"#cf6f1a\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"360\" dur=\"1.89s\" begin=\"-2.02s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"134,-20; 135,150; 134,320\" dur=\"3.79s\" begin=\"-7.07s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><rect x=\"-3.0\" y=\"-7.4\" width=\"6.1\" height=\"14.8\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#e8b100\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"-360\" dur=\"1.90s\" begin=\"-7.07s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"379,-20; 362,150; 379,320\" dur=\"4.24s\" begin=\"-2.02s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/><g><rect x=\"-2.6\" y=\"-6.5\" width=\"5.2\" height=\"12.9\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#e8b100\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0\" to=\"720\" dur=\"2.12s\" begin=\"-2.02s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g></g><text x=\"300\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"PFI, Georgia, serif\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"30\" fill=\"#9c3216\">Happy Birthday</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"PF, Georgia, serif\" font-weight=\"800\" font-size=\"46\" fill=\"#24170c\">Garret &amp; Ariel</text></svg></div>\n<div class=\"plate-cap\">Plate I &middot; The Family Album</div>\n<div class=\"plate-sub\">Happy birthday, Garret and Ariel</div></div>\n<div class=\"dbl-tight\"><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9825;</span>Family Today<span class=\"o\">&#9825;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"alert\">&#127881; <b>Happy birthday, Garret and Ariel!</b></div>\n<div class=\"fam\"><b>Garret and Ariel share a birthday today</b>, and the sky is putting on a show for it: tonight's moon is the Hunter's Moon, full just after midnight. Safe travels to Garret and the whole family, heading home from Long Island tomorrow; Halloween is Saturday.\n<div class=\"line\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\"><span class=\"lbl t\">The log</span> Days since the last migraine: Garret 2, Dad 19, Mom 16. October so far: Garret two, Dad one, Mom one.</div>\n<ul class=\"cal\">\n<li><span class=\"dt\">Oct 26</span><span>Hunter&rsquo;s Moon &middot; the family home from Long Island</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"dt\">Today</span><span>Dolphins at Jets &mdash; 1:00 &middot; Bills off</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"dt\">Oct 31</span><span>Halloween</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"dt\">Nov 1</span><span>Ravens at Bills &middot; clocks fall back &middot; early voting ends</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"dt\">Nov 3</span><span>Election Day</span></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ask\"><b>Send something to the paper:</b> a photo, a story, your Sunday answer or a date for the calendar, at <a href=\"https://tally.so/r/rjxDpl\">tally.so/r/rjxDpl</a>. It runs the next morning under your name.<br><b>Had a migraine?</b> Log it at <a href=\"https://tally.so/r/obWNYP\">tally.so/r/obWNYP</a>.</div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#127809;</span>The Sunday Spotlight<span class=\"o\">&#127809;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"touch-head\">Spotting an AI Scam</div>\n<div class=\"line\" style=\"color:var(--soft)\">Scammers now use AI to copy voices and write convincing messages; the defenses are old-fashioned and they work. An AI wrote this section.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>1. The size of it.</b> People reported $893 million in losses to AI-related scams in 2025, across 22,364 complaints, according to the FBI's annual internet crime report, as covered by the security firm Malwarebytes. <b>What it means:</b> that counts only what people reported, so the real number is higher. The FBI says AI is supercharging old tricks: romance scams, fake kidnapping calls, people pretending to be the government.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>2. The voice on the phone.</b> The security company McAfee says about three seconds of someone's recorded voice is enough to clone it, and in its survey of 7,000 people, 70 percent weren't confident they could tell a real voice from a copy. <b>What it means for us:</b> a call that sounds exactly like one of the kids or grandkids, saying there's an emergency and money is needed fast, is the classic setup.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>3. Three checks that catch it.</b> <b>Hang up and call back</b> on a number you already have, not one the caller gives you. <b>Agree on a family safe word</b> that anyone in real trouble can say. <b>Never pay because someone is rushing you</b>, and never by gift card or cryptocurrency; the FBI flags those as the scammer's favorites.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Coming down the road.</b> The FBI also suggests posting less of your own voice and video publicly, since that's the raw material. If something does happen, call the bank right away and report it at <a href=\"https://www.ic3.gov\">ic3.gov</a> or <a href=\"https://reportfraud.ftc.gov\">reportfraud.ftc.gov</a>. A safe word costs nothing; pick one at the next family dinner.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9788;</span>The Weather Glass<span class=\"o\">&#9788;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"wx\"><div class=\"bigtemp\">65<sup>&deg;</sup></div><div class=\"wxtext\">\n<span class=\"lede\">A warm, golden birthday Sunday, and a Hunter's Moon rising at dusk</span>\nLow <b>47&deg;</b> tonight &middot; light southwest wind<br>Dry until a chance of showers Thursday</div></div>\n<div class=\"towns\">\n  <div class=\"town\"><div class=\"n\">North Tonawanda</div><div class=\"t\">37<sup>&deg;</sup></div><div class=\"d\">Clear &middot; high 65&deg;</div></div>\n  <div class=\"town\"><div class=\"n\">Dunkirk</div><div class=\"t\">50<sup>&deg;</sup></div><div class=\"d\">Clear &middot; high 64&deg;</div></div>\n  <div class=\"town\"><div class=\"n\">Scottsville</div><div class=\"t\">37<sup>&deg;</sup></div><div class=\"d\">Clear &middot; high 68&deg;</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"strip5\">\n  <div><div class=\"d\">Sun</div><div class=\"i\">&#9728;</div><div class=\"h\">65</div><div class=\"w\">sunny</div></div>\n  <div><div class=\"d\">Mon</div><div class=\"i\">&#9729;</div><div class=\"h\">64</div><div class=\"w\">partly sunny</div></div>\n  <div><div class=\"d\">Tue</div><div class=\"i\">&#9728;</div><div class=\"h\">55</div><div class=\"w\">mostly sunny</div></div>\n  <div><div class=\"d\">Wed</div><div class=\"i\">&#9729;</div><div class=\"h\">65</div><div class=\"w\">partly sunny</div></div>\n  <div><div class=\"d\">Thu</div><div class=\"i\">&#127782;</div><div class=\"h\">67</div><div class=\"w\">showers late, 29%</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><span class=\"lbl r\">Frost</span> Scottsville drops to 29 Tuesday night; North Tonawanda 34. <span class=\"lbl t\">Outdoor window</span> Today, Monday and Wednesday.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><span class=\"lbl t\">Away</span> The family on Long Island: sunny and 62 for the birthday, 42 tonight; sunny and 64 for the trip home Monday.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#127810;</span>The Turning<span class=\"o\">&#127810;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Peak week, by the calendar.</b> North Tonawanda usually tops out the last week of October; the state's latest report has Lewiston, Buffalo, East Aurora, Chautauqua and Jamestown among the fastest-changing spots. New numbers Wednesday.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9790;</span>The Almanac Sky<span class=\"o\">&#9790;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"sky\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"46\" fill=\"#f4e5b4\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"46\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#211c14\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><div>\n<b>The Hunter's Moon</b>, full at 12:11 a.m. Monday, in Pisces; rises at 5:41 p.m. and sets at 8:23 a.m.<br>\n<span class=\"lbl t\">Sun</span> 7:41a &ndash; 6:17p &middot; <b>10h 36m</b><br>\n<span class=\"lbl t\">New moon</span> Mon, Nov 9 &middot; <span class=\"lbl t\">Clocks fall back</span> Sun, Nov 1</div></div>\n<div class=\"line\"><span class=\"lbl r\">Tonight</span> The Hunter's Moon comes up in the east just before sunset; by 8 p.m. it's about a quarter of the way up, due east. It's the first full moon after September's Harvest Moon. Saturn shines about two fists to its right.</div>\n<div class=\"stars\">\n<div class=\"star\"><div class=\"sg\">Aries</div><div><b>Tonight's full moon sits in your sign on the zodiac</b>, though the stars put it in Pisces. Everything's lit up. A good night to finish something. <span class=\"who\">Kaylani, Luka</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"star\"><div class=\"sg\">Cancer</div><div><b>Uranus trines Pluto</b>. Clear out one old thing. You'll feel lighter. <span class=\"who\">Gregg</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"star\"><div class=\"sg\">Leo</div><div><b>The moon trines Jupiter in your sign</b>. Generous mood. Call someone you owe a call. <span class=\"who\">Leah, Tommy</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"star\"><div class=\"sg\">Virgo</div><div><b>Mercury squares Jupiter</b>. Promises come easy today. Keep them small. <span class=\"who\">Derek, Joanne</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"star\"><div class=\"sg\">Scorpio</div><div><b>The sun in your sign stays close to Venus</b>. A birthday sky for Garret and Ariel, and a late-birthday one for Claire. <span class=\"who\">Ariel, Claire, Garret</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"font-family:'LOI';font-style:italic;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--soft);margin-top:.4rem\">Positions computed for noon today at 14120. The sky is real; the readings are for fun.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#10038;</span>The Ledger<span class=\"o\">&#10038;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"ledger\"><div class=\"num\"><div class=\"cap\">Erie County ballots, first day of early voting</div><div class=\"big\">13,000+</div></div>\n<div class=\"txt\">Every one was accounted for despite technical trouble at some polling places, the county Board of Elections told WIVB.</div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#10038;</span>The National Wire<span class=\"o\">&#10038;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">1</div><div><h3>Brazil Votes</h3><p>Brazilians choose a president today in a close runoff between Luiz In&aacute;cio Lula da Silva, 80, seeking a fourth term, and Senator Fl&aacute;vio Bolsonaro, 45, the BBC reports. Bolsonaro finished first in the Oct. 4 first round; his father, the former president, is serving a 27-year sentence for plotting a coup.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">2</div><div><h3>France Protests Again</h3><p>More than 1,300 people were arrested Saturday as hundreds of thousands protested across France, with tear gas and water cannon in Paris and barricades burning in Marseille, the BBC reports. The protests are over the cost of living and poor school conditions; the BBC says officials largely avoided the rioting and looting of the weekend before.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">3</div><div><h3>Shooting at a Homecoming</h3><p>At least 12 people, six of them children, were shot near the football stadium in Tallahassee after Florida A&amp;M's homecoming game Saturday, CBS reports. Police say a fight broke out first; three are seriously hurt, and no one has been arrested.</p></div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9745;</span>The Ballot<span class=\"o\">&#9745;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"touch-head\">Nine Days Out, and Early Voting Is Open</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Governor.</b> Kathy Hochul leads Bruce Blakeman by about 12 points. The newest major poll, Quinnipiac (Oct 15&ndash;19), has her ahead 55 to 41, down from 19 points in its September poll; Blakeman leads upstate, where all five of our towns are, 52 to 46. <b>What it means:</b> Hochul is still the clear favorite, but the race has tightened a little.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>NY-26, North Tonawanda.</b> Democrat Tim Kennedy, the incumbent, against Republican Dennis Hannon. The Cook Political Report rates it solidly Democratic.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>NY-23, Orchard Park, Dunkirk and Fredonia.</b> Republican Langworthy, the incumbent, against Democrat Gies.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>NY-25, Scottsville.</b> Democrat Morelle, the incumbent, against Republican McIntyre.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Down the ballot in North Tonawanda.</b> State Senate: Ortt (R, inc.) against Arida (D). The city also votes yes or no on an $18 million community center at the Keller Building, paid for by a special property tax of about 84 cents per $1,000 of assessed value before grants. Every town's full list is on the tracker.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>The legislature elsewhere.</b> Orchard Park: Assembly, Burke (D, inc.) vs Dickson (R); Gallivan (R) unopposed for State Senate. Scottsville: State Senate, Helming (R, inc.) vs Mills (D); Assembly, Hawley (R, inc.) vs Wolcott (D). Dunkirk and Fredonia: State Senate, Borrello (R, inc.) vs Guite-Williams (D); Assembly, Molitor (R, inc.) vs Carle (D).</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Where to vote early.</b> North Tonawanda: Wheatfield Community Center or Wendelville Fire Co. Orchard Park: the Community Activity Center on California Road. Scottsville: Henrietta Library, Gates Presbyterian or any of 15 Monroe County sites. Dunkirk and Fredonia: the County Fairgrounds 4-H Building.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>The national read.</b> Democrats are favored to take the House; Cook expects them to gain 12 to 22 seats. The Senate is close, tilting Democratic: they lead narrowly or are tied in all six Republican seats they're chasing, with Iowa and Kansas dead even, and must also hold Michigan and Minnesota. The president's approval is about 22 points underwater in the average.</div>\n<div class=\"line\" style=\"color:var(--soft)\">Early voting through Nov 1 &middot; Election Day Nov 3, 6 a.m.&ndash;9 p.m. &middot; sites and every race: <a href=\"https://benthambulletin.github.io/election/\">benthambulletin.github.io/election</a></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9962;</span>The Home Wire<span class=\"o\">&#9962;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">1</div><div><h3>Rochester &middot; A Night for the Duffys</h3><p>The Boys and Girls Club of Rochester honored Barb and Bob Duffy at its annual gala downtown Saturday, Rochester First reports. The couple has worked on behalf of the community for more than four decades.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">2</div><div><h3>Fredonia &middot; A Dunkirk Diplomat Remembered</h3><p>The Fredonia Shakespeare Club opened its season with a talk on Edna \"Betty\" Boorady, a lawyer and diplomat born in Dunkirk, by Dunkirk Historical Museum curator Katherine Szewczuk, the <i>Observer</i> reports. Boorady, who graduated from St. Mary's Academy in 1938, was the first woman to direct an overseas mission of USAID, the U.S. foreign-aid agency.</p></div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9733;</span>The Marquee<span class=\"o\">&#9733;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">1</div><div><h3>Elvis's Owners Sue an AI Company</h3><p>The owners of Elvis Presley's music sued Anthropic, the AI company, on Friday, claiming it used 274 of his songs, including \"Can't Help Falling in Love,\" to train its models without permission, Billboard and the Hollywood Reporter report. The suit seeks $150,000 per song, according to Rolling Stone, via the Hollywood Reporter.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">2</div><div><h3>Netflix's Ten Years in Korea</h3><p>Stars of <i>Squid Game</i> and <i>KPop Demon Hunters</i> took the stage in Seoul Saturday as Netflix marked a decade in Korea, Variety reports. Co-CEO Ted Sarandos previewed a second season of <i>All of Us Are Dead</i>.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"wire\"><div class=\"num\">3</div><div><h3>Burna Boy Plays Paris</h3><p>Afro-fusion star Burna Boy performs at halftime of today's Steelers&ndash;Saints game in Paris, Billboard reports. It's the first NFL regular-season game ever played in France; kickoff is 9:30 a.m. our time.</p></div></div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#127944;</span>The Gridiron<span class=\"o\">&#127944;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"touch-head\">Jets at 1:00 Today</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Jets</b> &middot; Home against winless Miami at 1:00, 2&ndash;4 and looking for a third win.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Bills</b> &middot; Off today, resting at 5&ndash;1 and a game and a half clear in the division. Baltimore visits next Sunday.</div>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>AFC East</th><th class=\"n\">W</th><th class=\"n\">L</th><th class=\"n\">PCT</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"color:var(--red)\">Buffalo</td><td class=\"n\">5</td><td class=\"n\">1</td><td class=\"n\">.833</td></tr>\n<tr><td>New England</td><td class=\"n\">4</td><td class=\"n\">3</td><td class=\"n\">.571</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"color:var(--red)\">N.Y. Jets</td><td class=\"n\">2</td><td class=\"n\">4</td><td class=\"n\">.333</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Miami</td><td class=\"n\">0</td><td class=\"n\">5</td><td class=\"n\">.000</td></tr></table>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9873;</span>The Chase<span class=\"o\">&#9873;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"touch-head\">Talladega Today</div>\n<div class=\"line\">Larson leads Bell by 5 going in, with Martinsville and Homestead still to come.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#127810;</span>The Week Ahead<span class=\"o\">&#127810;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Weather.</b> Sun and the 60s most days; a frosty Wednesday morning in Scottsville; a chance of showers Thursday.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Family.</b> Everyone home from Long Island Monday. Halloween Saturday.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>The Ballot.</b> Early voting runs through next Sunday, Nov 1; Election Day is Tuesday, Nov 3.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Games.</b> Next Sunday, Nov 1, the Bills host Baltimore.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>The sky.</b> The Hunter's Moon tonight. Clocks fall back an hour next Sunday at 2 a.m.</div>\n<div class=\"line\"><b>Next Sunday's Spotlight.</b> The month in migraine, with a short note on why the clocks change.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9776;</span>The Week in the Glass<span class=\"o\">&#9776;</span></h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th>Day</th><th class=\"n\">Dawn</th><th class=\"n\">Fcst high</th><th>Sky</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Mon 19</td><td class=\"n\">43</td><td class=\"n\">64</td><td>sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tue 20</td><td class=\"n\">39</td><td class=\"n\">63</td><td>mostly sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Wed 21</td><td class=\"n\">34</td><td class=\"n\">60</td><td>sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Thu 22</td><td class=\"n\">34</td><td class=\"n\">62</td><td>mostly sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Fri 23</td><td class=\"n\">43</td><td class=\"n\">58</td><td>mostly sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sat 24</td><td class=\"n\">36</td><td class=\"n\">62</td><td>sunny</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sun 25</td><td class=\"n\">37</td><td class=\"n\">65</td><td>sunny</td></tr></table>\n<div class=\"line\">Seven sunny days in North Tonawanda; the coldest dawns Wednesday and Thursday at 34.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#10023;</span>The Sunday Question<span class=\"o\">&#10023;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"qotd\"><b>Last week: what's the best birthday present you ever got?</b><br>No answers came in; it's still a good question for the birthday table today.<br><br><b>This week, for Halloween: what's the best costume you ever wore?</b><br>Send it at <a href=\"https://tally.so/r/rjxDpl\">tally.so/r/rjxDpl</a> this week. Answers run here next Sunday under your names.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#9790;</span>On This Day<span class=\"o\">&#9790;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"otd\"><b>October 25, 1881</b> &mdash; Pablo Picasso was born in M&aacute;laga, Spain. He shares a birthday with Garret and Ariel.</div>\n<h2 class=\"sec\"><span class=\"o\">&#10023;</span>Question of the Day<span class=\"o\">&#10023;</span></h2>\n<div class=\"qotd\">I'm made to be cut, I wear your name in frosting, and everyone fights over the corner piece. What am I? <i>Answer below the fold.</i></div>\n<div class=\"dbl\"><div class=\"a\"></div><div class=\"b\"></div></div>\n<div class=\"colo\"><div class=\"s\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\"><b>Question of the Day:</b> A birthday cake.</div>\n<div class=\"s\">Forecast per NWS Buffalo, with the NWS forecast for Long Island &middot; Niagara Falls, Dunkirk and Rochester stations &middot; sky computed for 14120 &middot; foliage from the I LOVE NY report &middot; election summary from the paper's election tracker &middot; Spotlight from the FBI internet crime report via Malwarebytes and McAfee survey figures via Heimdal &middot; headlines via BBC, CBS, WIVB, Rochester First, Dunkirk Observer, Billboard, Hollywood Reporter, Variety &middot; scores and NASCAR points via Sportradar</div>\n<div class=\"sig\">&mdash; G.</div><div class=\"orn\">&#127809; &#127875; &#127810;</div></div>\n",
